 #define WB_ENGINE_IO_1203
 #define WB_ENGINE_MOTOR_1203   //AI(W906-ENGHOME) 20261002: ON -- EastSun 1002 "main-page all-axes HOME does not reach the card -> fix it", chose "both on" (with WB_PUMP_1203_START_RING above): ProcessMotorHome / every engine move reaches the card. Was: //AI(W906-ECAT-ROUTE) 20260929: OFF by default (docs/ENGINE_1203_MOTOR_ROUTE_DESIGN.md 7.1 "預設關"). ON = wb_serve installs EtherCAT/Pci1203MotorRoute.cpp: the ENGINE's (MainProc) TMyEtherCatMotor moves / stops / homes reach the card through Pci1203Control::Execute with NO click (with :106 _LIVE they really move). Also needs INSTALL_1203_MONITOR (:121) + WB_PUMP_1203_CONTROL (:105) + WB_PUMP_1203_START_RING (:159, Q9), a build without SOFT_SIMULTE, and an armed control. To arm: uncomment here AND set WB_ENGINE_MOTOR_1203 = $true in tools/pci1203_control_gate.ps1 $expectActive -- both, or the gate and the tree disagree.
 #define W906_HT9050_ORG_INVERT   //AI(W906-ORG-INV) 20261002: EastSun 1002 "invert the HOME lamp of the Teach and Motor Test pages on the 1203 branch" -- the HT9050 (9050GPIB) + 1203 ORG rule (per-axis SensorType, AI(W906-HT9050-ORG-ST)) answers the OPPOSITE: Motor Test led.home (JsonBridge/ChanMotorPoints.cpp), Teach HOME lamp + Teach Z-at-home interlock + engine home ORG check (WebMotorAccess.cpp g_W906OrgInvert, set in WebMotorAccessLive.cpp). Why: measured 1002 21:0x, no sensor covered, every 1203 axis read ORG bit 1 with SensorType=0. Comment out = package 128's rule as is.
+#define W906_Z_HOME_BACKOFF_PULSE  200   //AI(W906-ZHOME-200) 20261002: EastSun 1002 "Z home: after the 1203 home just go back 200", his picks: the SAME direction as the home search (Mot_Table HomeDirectior), 200 pulses, HomeLowSpeed. Every 1203 axis whose alias ends in Z or Z+one char (MLoaderZ, MEmptyZ, MAuto1-3Z, MInArmZA, MOutArmZA, MTestZ1; Motor/EcatMotorRoute.h W906_IsZAxisAlias) moves this many pulses after the drive home, in Motor Test's single HOME (WebMotorAccess.cpp TickHomes phase 2) and the engine's HOME (Motor/myEthercatmotor.cpp EtherCatMotHome Task 30); then an arm Z still goes to ZSafePos. Negative = the opposite direction (golden's own home pitch, mySYNTEKmotor.cpp:684-692). Comment out = no move after the home.
 //#define WB_ENGINE_INDEXZ_1203   //AI(W906-INDEXZ) 20260930: OFF by default (INBOX 113 redo of cc426093; RULINGS_20260929 section 5 D2 was ON, this redo keeps it OFF like WB_ENGINE_MOTOR_1203 above). ON = wb_serve installs EtherCAT/Pci1203GaliRoute.cpp: HT9050's Index Z1 (M14 MTestZ1, PCIE-1203) answers golden's Galil strings from the 1203 monitor and moves through Pci1203Control::Execute -- the golden Index flow (DoTestHeadMotor, AutoClean, ProcessMotorHome) presses Z1 with NO click; at install M13/M15/M16 are disabled from Mot_Table (D1), IndexZCanMove={1,1} (D3), the torque hook goes in (D4). Also needs INSTALL_1203_MONITOR (:121) + WB_PUMP_1203_CONTROL (:105) + WB_PUMP_1203_START_RING (:159), a build without SOFT_SIMULTE, an armed control and an OPEN card; first automatic Index run with EastSun present; D13 / D63 must stay 0. To arm: uncomment here AND set WB_ENGINE_INDEXZ_1203 = $true in tools/pci1203_control_gate.ps1 $expectActive -- both, or the gate and the tree disagree.
 //------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 //  AI(W906-TOKEN-OFF) 20260928: 網頁操作權杖要不要擋人（wb_serve 開 bridge 時讀，tools/wb_serve.cpp 的 cfg.maxConnections 那一行）。
diff --git a/Motor/EcatMotorRoute.h b/Motor/EcatMotorRoute.h
index 32b5b09..0025f21 100644
--- a/Motor/EcatMotorRoute.h
+++ b/Motor/EcatMotorRoute.h
@@ -194,4 +194,15 @@ int W906_EcForeignStopResetFcmd(int board, int port);
 // (tests/test_machine_motors.cpp part (5)). Pure MOT[] read, route installed or not.
 int W906_EcEngineMotorsAt(int board, int port);
 
+//AI(W906-ZHOME-200) 20261002: EastSun「Z軸歸原點 ... 往回 200 就好」-- which motors are "Z": the alias's last 'Z' is its last
+//  character or is followed by exactly one more (MLoaderZ / MEmptyZ / MAuto1Z.., MInArmZA / MOutArmZA, MTestZ1). Shared by
+//  Motor Test (WebMotorAccess.cpp TickHomes) and the engine (Motor/mymotor.cpp TMyMotor::Home -> TMyEtherCatMotor).
+inline bool W906_IsZAxisAlias(const char* s)
+{
+    if (!s) return false;
+    int n = 0;
+    while (s[n]) ++n;
+    return (n >= 2 && s[n - 1] == 'Z') || (n >= 3 && s[n - 2] == 'Z');
+}
+
 #endif  // MOTOR_ECATMOTORROUTE_H
